-- 027: the parks and coasters a friend's ranking sheet needed that we did not
-- have (2026-10-04). Carter: "Yes please for this list".
--
-- Source: "Nerd Sheet v2" (886 rows, mostly UK and Europe), matched against the
-- LIVE tables (read through the D1 connector, not the stale snapshot). Before
-- this, 298 rows could not be matched: 253 at 89 parks we lacked, the rest at
-- parks we have but missing the coaster. After it, 17 rows stay unmatched, all
-- on purpose: "Travelling" with no showman named, a backyard coaster, "900"
-- with no park, two US family centres with no town, and seven Adventureland
-- rows that /import will ask about (we have Adventureland in Iowa AND New York).
--
-- What goes in:
--  * 79 parks. Pins for the ones with a fixed address; play areas, small
--    venues and travelling showmen get none, like Butler Amusements already.
--    Travelling coasters sit under "<Showman> (travelling)".
--  * 256 coasters. Maker, type and model are the sheet's (its rider knows these
--    rides), mapped to the names the table already uses ("Mack" -> MACK Rides,
--    "Tivoli" -> Zierer Tivoli). Opening years only where certain; the rest are
--    left blank for /edit rather than guessed.
--  * 30 coasters at parks we already had (Zadra, Valkyria, Monster, Colossos,
--    Hansa-Park's five, Grand National's right-hand track copied from its left …).
--    Rides the sheet only spells differently are NOT added again; /import's
--    fuzzy match already finds "The Big One" as Big One.
--  * Park aliases for the sheet's spellings (Hansa Park, Flamingoland, DLP -
--    Studios …) and coaster aliases for a few (Colossos: Kampf Der Giganten).
--  * Map pins for six UK parks someone added through /add without one.
--
-- Safe to run twice: every park and coaster is matched on name (+ park) before
-- it goes in, aliases on the pair, and pins only where lat is still empty.
-- Ids are MAX(id)+1 per row, the same rule POST /api/coaster uses.
-- Dry run against a copy of the live tables: parks 261 -> 340, coasters
-- 1214 -> 1470; a second run changed nothing.
--
-- Raw SQL skips the Worker, so run Actions -> "Sync static JSON from D1" after.
--
-- Run it with:  npx wrangler d1 execute coasterhub --remote --file=migrations/027-uk-europe-parks.sql
-- (388 statements is a lot for the console's one-line box.)
--
-- Check after:
--   SELECT COUNT(*) FROM parks;      -- 340
--   SELECT COUNT(*) FROM coasters;   -- 1470
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO coaster_aliases (coaster_id, former_name, note, added) SELECT id, 'Toos Express', 'import 027', date('now') FROM coasters WHERE name = 'Toos-Express' AND park = 'Toverland';
